---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GlassPanel from '../components/ui/GlassPanel.astro';
---

<Layout title="About | Ryan Wolfe" description="A little context, minus the portfolio theater.">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    <GlassPanel class="md:col-span-2 p-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">About</h1>
      <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <p>
          I’m Ryan — a staff engineer. I’m drawn to the messy boundary where software meets reality:
          systems, tradeoffs, and the human behaviors that quietly determine whether the technical stuff works.
        </p>

        <p>
          In my day job I’m focused on infrastructure programmability and automation.
          Outside of that, I write about engineering leadership, developer productivity systems,
          and the builder’s psychology — the “soft” skills that are usually just unpriced technical risk.
        </p>

        <p>
          This site is a writing hub. If you want the guided tour, start with <a href="/start">Start here</a>.
          If you want the unpolished version of my brain, <a href="/notes">Notes</a> is where things go to ferment.
        </p>

        <h2>What I optimize for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Leverage</strong> (outcomes over activity)</li>
          <li><strong>Clarity</strong> (models, constraints, and definitions of done)</li>
          <li><strong>Craft</strong> (quality without martyrdom)</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          By day I'm a staff engineer at Google working on cloud infrastructure — large-scale
          networking and the platforms that operate it. Before that: a decade in network and
          security consulting, and the Marine Corps before that. On my own time I build and
          operate an autonomous software estate — a fleet of coding agents that design, ship,
          and run real products, with me as the operator (<a href="/work">the numbers</a>).
        </p>
      </div>
    </GlassPanel>

    <GlassPanel class="p-8 flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center">
      <div class="w-32 h-32 bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-full mb-6 overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/profile.jpeg" alt="Profile" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-1">Contact</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-6">If you want to reach me, email is best.</p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="w-full py-3 bg-brand-600 hover:bg-brand-700 text-white rounded-xl font-medium transition-colors flex items-center justify-center gap-2"
      >
        <Icon name="lucide:mail" class="w-4 h-4" />
        Contact
      </a>
    </GlassPanel>
  </div>

  <GlassPanel class="mt-6 p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Quick facts</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
      A few things that are true, without turning this into a resume.
    </p>

    <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      <li class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl">Staff Software Engineer @ Google</li>
      <li class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl">Background in network/security + automation</li>
      <li class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl">Former US Marine Corps (IT / operations)</li>
      <li class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl">Writing first: essays + notes</li>
    </ul>

  </GlassPanel>
</Layout>
